    "created_at": "2024-12-11T02:55:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-12-11T02:55:44Z",
    "body": "> Yeah, I think there is an additional check we need to do if URL's blob entry is null - we can hit this case for the following test:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> window.open('blob:https://video_url');\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nThe steps for this one are that [URL parsing](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#url-parsing) will not set URL blob entry to a value if not found in the blob registry lookup:\r\n\r\n> Set url’s [blob URL entry](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url-blob-entry) to the result of [resolving the blob URL](https://w3c.github.io/FileAPI/#blob-url-resolve) url, if that did not return failure, and null otherwise.\r\n\r\nSo we can't rely on the URL blob entry being null if only the blob is set, so should be treated like perhaps in the [URL origin serialization](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#origin) steps",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
